@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `br-interpretation-time`

-- Decreto-Lei 4.657/1942 (LINDB), arts. 7 to 19: which country's law governs, which courts and authorities are competent,
-- and when a foreign judgment or act has effect in Brazil.
-- A country is a STRING the caller supplies. A rule that names a connecting factor returns the country that factor points to;
-- a rule that is a condition returns TRUE or FALSE. Where a paragraph covers only some cases and says nothing of the others,
-- the other cases are a named REFUSE, and a rule that PERMITS something is named "allows", so that FALSE reads "this article
-- does not give it" and not "this article forbids it".

§ `LINDB arts. 7 to 19: private international law and consular acts`

§§ `Art. 7: persons, family and marriage`

-- src:27 | Art. 7o A lei do país em que domiciliada a pessoa determina as regras sobre o começo e o fim da personalidade, o nome, a capacidade e os direitos de família.
-- src:28 | § 1o Realizando-se o casamento no Brasil, será aplicada a lei brasileira quanto aos impedimentos dirimentes e às formalidades da celebração.
-- src:29 | § 2o O casamento de estrangeiros poderá celebrar-se perante autoridades diplomáticas ou consulares do país de ambos os nubentes.
-- src:30 | § 3o Tendo os nubentes domicílio diverso, regerá os casos de invalidade do matrimônio a lei do primeiro domicílio conjugal.
-- src:31 | § 4o O regime de bens, legal ou convencional, obedece à lei do país em que tiverem os nubentes domicílio, e, se este for diverso, a do primeiro domicílio conjugal.
-- src:32 | § 5º - O estrangeiro casado, que se naturalizar brasileiro, pode, mediante expressa anuência de seu cônjuge, requerer ao juiz, no ato de entrega do decreto de naturalização, se apostile ao mesmo a adoção do regime de comunhão parcial de bens, respeitados os direitos de terceiros e dada esta adoção ao competente registro.
-- src:33 | § 6⟦STRUCK: º⟧ O divórcio realizado no estrangeiro, se um ou ambos os cônjuges forem brasileiros, só será reconhecido no Brasil depois de 1 (um) ano da data da sentença, salvo se houver sido antecedida de separação judicial por igual prazo, caso em que a homologação produzirá efeito imediato, obedecidas as condições estabelecidas para a eficácia das sentenças estrangeiras no país. O Superior Tribunal de Justiça, na forma de seu regimento interno, poderá reexaminar, a requerimento do interessado, decisões já proferidas em pedidos de homologação de sentenças estrangeiras de divórcio de brasileiros, a fim de que passem a produzir todos os efeitos legais.
-- src:34 | § 7o Salvo o caso de abandono, o domicílio do chefe da família estende-se ao outro cônjuge e aos filhos não emancipados, e o do tutor ou curador aos incapazes sob sua guarda.
-- src:35 | § 8o Quando a pessoa não tiver domicílio, considerar-se-á domiciliada no lugar de sua residência ou naquele em que se encontre.
@ref LINDB art. 7 caput to par. 8 (src:27-35)
GIVEN domicile IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`the country whose law governs personality, name, capacity and family rights, for a person domiciled in` domicile MEANS domicile

@ref LINDB art. 7 par. 1 (src:28)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`art. 7 par. 1 speaks only of a marriage celebrated in Brazil` MEANS
    REFUSE "art. 7 par. 1 speaks only of a marriage celebrated in Brazil and says nothing of one celebrated elsewhere"

@ref LINDB art. 7 par. 1 (src:28)
GIVEN `the country where the marriage is celebrated` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`the country whose law governs the diriment impediments and the formalities of celebration of a marriage celebrated in` `the country where the marriage is celebrated` MEANS
    IF `the country where the marriage is celebrated` EQUALS "Brazil"
    THEN "Brazil"
    ELSE `art. 7 par. 1 speaks only of a marriage celebrated in Brazil`

-- Par. 2 permits; it does not forbid anything else. FALSE means that par. 2 does not itself allow the celebration.
@ref LINDB art. 7 par. 2 (src:29)
GIVEN `the country of the first spouse` IS A STRING
      `the country of the second spouse` IS A STRING
      `the country the diplomatic or consular authority represents` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 7 par. 2 allows the marriage of foreigners before the diplomatic or consular authority of` `the country of the first spouse` `and` `the country of the second spouse` `,` `the country the diplomatic or consular authority represents` MEANS
        `the country of the first spouse` EQUALS `the country of the second spouse`
    AND `the country of the first spouse` EQUALS `the country the diplomatic or consular authority represents`
    AND NOT (`the country of the first spouse` EQUALS "Brazil")

@ref LINDB art. 7 par. 3 (src:30)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`art. 7 par. 3 speaks only of spouses with different domiciles` MEANS
    REFUSE "art. 7 par. 3 speaks only of spouses whose domiciles differ and says nothing of the invalidity of a marriage between spouses with the same domicile"

@ref LINDB art. 7 par. 3 (src:30)
GIVEN `the first spouse's domicile` IS A STRING
      `the second spouse's domicile` IS A STRING
      `the first conjugal domicile` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`the country whose law governs the invalidity of a marriage, for spouses domiciled in` `the first spouse's domicile` `and` `the second spouse's domicile` `with a first conjugal domicile in` `the first conjugal domicile` MEANS
    IF `the first spouse's domicile` EQUALS `the second spouse's domicile`
    THEN `art. 7 par. 3 speaks only of spouses with different domiciles`
    ELSE `the first conjugal domicile`

@ref LINDB art. 7 par. 4 (src:31)
GIVEN `the first spouse's domicile` IS A STRING
      `the second spouse's domicile` IS A STRING
      `the first conjugal domicile` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`the country whose law governs the regime of property, for spouses domiciled in` `the first spouse's domicile` `and` `the second spouse's domicile` `with a first conjugal domicile in` `the first conjugal domicile` MEANS
    IF `the first spouse's domicile` EQUALS `the second spouse's domicile`
    THEN `the first spouse's domicile`
    ELSE `the first conjugal domicile`

-- Par. 5: the rights of third parties are respected and the adoption is registered. Those are conditions on the annotation, not on
-- the request, and are not conditions of this predicate; the request is made to the judge at the delivery of the naturalisation decree.
@ref LINDB art. 7 par. 5 (src:32)
GIVEN `the spouse was a foreigner and is married` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the spouse has naturalised as a Brazilian` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other spouse has expressly consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is made at the delivery of the naturalisation decree` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 7 par. 5 allows a request that the adoption of the regime of partial community of property be noted` `the spouse was a foreigner and is married` `the spouse has naturalised as a Brazilian` `the other spouse has expressly consented` `the request is made at the delivery of the naturalisation decree` MEANS
        `the spouse was a foreigner and is married`
    AND `the spouse has naturalised as a Brazilian`
    AND `the other spouse has expressly consented`
    AND `the request is made at the delivery of the naturalisation decree`

@ref LINDB art. 7 par. 6 (src:33)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`art. 7 par. 6 speaks only of a divorce where one or both spouses are Brazilian` MEANS
    REFUSE "art. 7 par. 6 speaks only of a foreign divorce where one or both spouses are Brazilian"

@ref LINDB art. 7 par. 6 (src:33)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text does not say whether the anniversary day is itself after one year` MEANS
    REFUSE "art. 7 par. 6 says recognition comes only after 1 year from the date of the judgment, and the text does not say whether the anniversary day is itself after that year"

-- Par. 6, first sentence: a foreign divorce, where one or both spouses are Brazilian, is recognised in Brazil only after 1 year from the
-- date of the judgment, unless a judicial separation for an equal term came first, in which case the homologation takes immediate effect.
-- This answers the waiting rule only; the conditions for the efficacy of a foreign judgment are art. 15's.
@ref LINDB art. 7 par. 6 (src:33)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      judgment IS A DATE
      `one or both spouses are Brazilian` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a judicial separation for an equal term came first` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the waiting rule of art. 7 par. 6 is met on` d judgment `one or both spouses are Brazilian` `a judicial separation for an equal term came first` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `one or both spouses are Brazilian` THEN `art. 7 par. 6 speaks only of a divorce where one or both spouses are Brazilian`
        IF `a judicial separation for an equal term came first` THEN TRUE
        IF d LESS THAN `the anniversary of the judgment` THEN FALSE
        IF d GREATER THAN `the anniversary of the judgment` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE `the text does not say whether the anniversary day is itself after one year`
    WHERE
        `the anniversary of the judgment` MEANS `the day` 1 `years after` judgment

-- Par. 6, second sentence: the Superior Tribunal de Justica may, at the request of the interested person, re-examine decisions already
-- given on the homologation of foreign divorces of Brazilians, so that they come to produce all legal effects.
@ref LINDB art. 7 par. 6 (src:33)
GIVEN `the interested person has asked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision was given on the homologation of a foreign divorce of Brazilians` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 7 par. 6 allows the Superior Tribunal de Justica to re-examine the decision` `the interested person has asked` `the decision was given on the homologation of a foreign divorce of Brazilians` MEANS
        `the interested person has asked`
    AND `the decision was given on the homologation of a foreign divorce of Brazilians`

@ref LINDB art. 7 par. 7 (src:34)
DECLARE `A person's situation for art. 7 par. 7` HAS
    `the domicile the person has of their own`                                    IS A STRING
    `the person is the other spouse of the head of the family`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is an unemancipated child of the head of the family`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the domicile of the head of the family`                                       IS A STRING
    `the person is an incapable person under a guardian or curator`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the domicile of the guardian or curator`                                      IS A STRING
    `there is a case of abandonment`                                               IS A BOOLEAN

@ref LINDB art. 7 par. 7 (src:34)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text does not say which extension prevails` MEANS
    REFUSE "art. 7 par. 7 extends the domicile of the head of the family and that of the guardian or curator, and the text does not say which prevails for a person within both"

-- Par. 7: "Salvo o caso de abandono" opens the sentence and is taken to govern both extensions. Who is the head of the family,
-- and who abandoned whom, are not said; the caller says, by supplying the head's domicile and whether there is a case of abandonment.
@ref LINDB art. 7 par. 7 (src:34)
GIVEN p IS A `A person's situation for art. 7 par. 7`
GIVETH A STRING
`the domicile of the person under art. 7 par. 7` p MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF p's `there is a case of abandonment` THEN p's `the domicile the person has of their own`
        IF     `within the family extension`
           AND p's `the person is an incapable person under a guardian or curator`
           AND NOT (p's `the domicile of the head of the family` EQUALS p's `the domicile of the guardian or curator`)
        THEN `the text does not say which extension prevails`
        IF `within the family extension` THEN p's `the domicile of the head of the family`
        IF p's `the person is an incapable person under a guardian or curator` THEN p's `the domicile of the guardian or curator`
        OTHERWISE p's `the domicile the person has of their own`
    WHERE
        `within the family extension` MEANS
               p's `the person is the other spouse of the head of the family`
            OR p's `the person is an unemancipated child of the head of the family`

@ref LINDB art. 7 par. 8 (src:35)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text does not say which of residence and the place where found prevails` MEANS
    REFUSE "art. 7 par. 8 says residence or the place where the person is found, and the text does not say which prevails for a person who has a residence elsewhere"

-- Par. 8: a person with no domicile is considered domiciled at the place of residence or at the place where found.
-- A person with a residence is taken to have it as domicile, the place where found being the fallback; where a residence exists
-- and the person is found elsewhere the text does not say which counts, and that is refused.
@ref LINDB art. 7 par. 8 (src:35)
GIVEN residence IS A MAYBE STRING
      `the place where the person is found` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`the domicile of a person who has none, with a residence` residence `and found in` `the place where the person is found` MEANS
    CONSIDER residence
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the place where the person is found`
    WHEN JUST r THEN
        IF r EQUALS `the place where the person is found`
        THEN r
        ELSE `the text does not say which of residence and the place where found prevails`

§§ `Art. 8: property`

-- src:36 | Art. 8o Para qualificar os bens e regular as relações a eles concernentes, aplicar-se-á a lei do país em que estiverem situados.
-- src:37 | § 1o Aplicar-se-á a lei do país em que for domiciliado o proprietário, quanto aos bens moveis que ele trouxer ou se destinarem a transporte para outros lugares.
-- src:38 | § 2o O penhor regula-se pela lei do domicílio que tiver a pessoa, em cuja posse se encontre a coisa apenhada.
@ref LINDB art. 8 caput to par. 2 (src:36-38)
DECLARE `Property, for art. 8` IS ONE OF
    `property in general`
    `a movable the owner brings or means to carry to other places`
    `a thing in pledge`

-- Caput: the law of the country where the property is situated qualifies it and regulates the relations concerning it.
-- Par. 1: for movables the owner brings or means to carry elsewhere, the law of the country where the owner is domiciled.
-- Par. 2: the pledge is regulated by the law of the domicile of the person in whose possession the pledged thing is.
@ref LINDB art. 8 caput, par. 1, par. 2 (src:36-38)
GIVEN kind IS A `Property, for art. 8`
      `the country where it is situated` IS A STRING
      `the country where the owner is domiciled` IS A STRING
      `the country where the possessor of the pledged thing is domiciled` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`the country whose law governs property` kind `situated in` `the country where it is situated` `owned by one domiciled in` `the country where the owner is domiciled` `possessed by one domiciled in` `the country where the possessor of the pledged thing is domiciled` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `property in general` THEN `the country where it is situated`
    WHEN `a movable the owner brings or means to carry to other places` THEN `the country where the owner is domiciled`
    WHEN `a thing in pledge` THEN `the country where the possessor of the pledged thing is domiciled`

§§ `Art. 9: obligations`

-- src:39 | Art. 9o Para qualificar e reger as obrigações, aplicar-se-á a lei do país em que se constituirem.
-- src:40 | § 1o Destinando-se a obrigação a ser executada no Brasil e dependendo de forma essencial, será esta observada, admitidas as peculiaridades da lei estrangeira quanto aos requisitos extrínsecos do ato.
-- src:41 | § 2o A obrigação resultante do contrato reputa-se constituida no lugar em que residir o proponente.
@ref LINDB art. 9 caput to par. 2 (src:39-41)
GIVEN `the country where the obligation is constituted` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`the country whose law qualifies and governs an obligation constituted in` `the country where the obligation is constituted` MEANS
    `the country where the obligation is constituted`

-- Par. 2: an obligation resulting from a contract is deemed constituted at the place where the proponent resides.
@ref LINDB art. 9 par. 2 (src:41)
GIVEN `the country where the proponent resides` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`the country in which an obligation resulting from a contract is deemed constituted, the proponent residing in` `the country where the proponent resides` MEANS
    `the country where the proponent resides`

-- Par. 1: an obligation to be performed in Brazil that depends on an essential form: that form is observed,
-- admitting the peculiarities of the foreign law as to the extrinsic requirements of the act.
@ref LINDB art. 9 par. 1 (src:40)
GIVEN `the obligation is to be performed in Brazil` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the obligation depends on an essential form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the essential form of Brazilian law is observed under art. 9 par. 1` `the obligation is to be performed in Brazil` `the obligation depends on an essential form` MEANS
    `the obligation is to be performed in Brazil` AND `the obligation depends on an essential form`

@ref LINDB art. 9 par. 1 (src:40)
GIVEN `the obligation is to be performed in Brazil` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the obligation depends on an essential form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peculiarity concerns an extrinsic requirement of the act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 9 par. 1 admits a peculiarity of the foreign law` `the obligation is to be performed in Brazil` `the obligation depends on an essential form` `the peculiarity concerns an extrinsic requirement of the act` MEANS
        `the essential form of Brazilian law is observed under art. 9 par. 1` `the obligation is to be performed in Brazil` `the obligation depends on an essential form`
    AND `the peculiarity concerns an extrinsic requirement of the act`

§§ `Art. 10: succession`

-- src:42 | Art. 10. A sucessão por morte ou por ausência obedece à lei do país em que domiciliado o defunto ou o desaparecido, qualquer que seja a natureza e a situação dos bens.
-- src:43 | § 1º A sucessão de bens de estrangeiros, situados no País, será regulada pela lei brasileira em benefício do cônjuge ou dos filhos brasileiros, ou de quem os represente, sempre que não lhes seja mais favorável a lei pessoal do de cujus.
-- src:44 | § 2o A lei do domicílio do herdeiro ou legatário regula a capacidade para suceder.
@ref LINDB art. 10 caput to par. 2 (src:42-44)
GIVEN `the country where the deceased or missing person was domiciled` IS A STRING
      `the deceased was a foreigner with assets situated in Brazil` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a Brazilian spouse or child, or one who represents them, benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal law of the deceased is more favourable to them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
`the country whose law governs a succession` `the country where the deceased or missing person was domiciled` `the deceased was a foreigner with assets situated in Brazil` `a Brazilian spouse or child, or one who represents them, benefits` `the personal law of the deceased is more favourable to them` MEANS
    IF     `the deceased was a foreigner with assets situated in Brazil`
       AND `a Brazilian spouse or child, or one who represents them, benefits`
       AND NOT `the personal law of the deceased is more favourable to them`
    THEN "Brazil"
    ELSE `the country where the deceased or missing person was domiciled`

@ref LINDB art. 10 par. 2 (src:44)
GIVEN `the country where the heir or legatee is domiciled` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`the country whose law governs the capacity to succeed, the heir or legatee being domiciled in` `the country where the heir or legatee is domiciled` MEANS
    `the country where the heir or legatee is domiciled`

§§ `Art. 11: organisations and foreign governments`

-- src:45 | Art. 11. As organizações destinadas a fins de interesse coletivo, como as sociedades e as fundações, obedecem à lei do Estado em que se constituirem.
-- src:46 | § 1o Não poderão, entretanto ter no Brasil filiais, agências ou estabelecimentos antes de serem os atos constitutivos aprovados pelo Governo brasileiro, ficando sujeitas à lei brasileira.
-- src:47 | § 2o Os Governos estrangeiros, bem como as organizações de qualquer natureza, que eles tenham constituido, dirijam ou hajam investido de funções públicas, não poderão adquirir no Brasil bens imóveis ou susceptiveis de desapropriação.
-- src:48 | § 3o Os Governos estrangeiros podem adquirir a propriedade dos prédios necessários à sede dos representantes diplomáticos ou dos agentes consulares.
@ref LINDB art. 11 caput to par. 3 (src:45-48)
GIVEN `the country where the organisation was constituted` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`the country whose law governs an organisation constituted in` `the country where the organisation was constituted` MEANS
    `the country where the organisation was constituted`

-- Par. 1: no branch, agency or establishment in Brazil before the constitutive acts are approved by the Brazilian Government.
-- This is a prohibition: TRUE means par. 1 forbids it; FALSE means par. 1 does not.
@ref LINDB art. 11 par. 1 (src:46)
GIVEN `the constitutive acts have been approved by the Brazilian Government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 11 par. 1 forbids a branch, agency or establishment in Brazil` `the constitutive acts have been approved by the Brazilian Government` MEANS
    NOT `the constitutive acts have been approved by the Brazilian Government`

-- Par. 1, last words: the organisations remain subject to Brazilian law.
@ref LINDB art. 11 par. 1 (src:46)
GIVETH A STRING
`the country whose law an organisation with a branch in Brazil is subject to` MEANS "Brazil"

-- Par. 2: foreign governments, and organisations of any nature they constituted, direct or have invested with public functions,
-- may not acquire in Brazil real property or property susceptible to expropriation. TRUE means par. 2 forbids it.
@ref LINDB art. 11 par. 2 (src:47)
GIVEN `it is a foreign government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an organisation a foreign government constituted, directs or has invested with public functions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is real property or susceptible to expropriation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 11 par. 2 forbids the acquisition` `it is a foreign government` `it is an organisation a foreign government constituted, directs or has invested with public functions` `the property is real property or susceptible to expropriation` MEANS
        (   `it is a foreign government`
         OR `it is an organisation a foreign government constituted, directs or has invested with public functions`)
    AND `the property is real property or susceptible to expropriation`

-- Par. 3: foreign governments may acquire the buildings needed for the seat of diplomatic representatives or consular agents.
-- FALSE means par. 3 does not allow it, not that it forbids it. An organisation of a foreign government is not within par. 3.
@ref LINDB art. 11 par. 3 (src:48)
GIVEN `it is a foreign government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the building is needed for the seat of diplomatic representatives or consular agents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 11 par. 3 allows the acquisition` `it is a foreign government` `the building is needed for the seat of diplomatic representatives or consular agents` MEANS
    `it is a foreign government` AND `the building is needed for the seat of diplomatic representatives or consular agents`

@ref LINDB art. 11 par. 2, par. 3 (src:47-48)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`neither par. 2 nor par. 3 of art. 11 speaks to this acquisition` MEANS
    REFUSE "neither par. 2 nor par. 3 of art. 11 speaks to this acquisition"

-- Par. 3 is read as the exception to par. 2 for the diplomatic and consular seat, and is tried first. The text does not state
-- which prevails (fork F-11); this order is the encoding's.
@ref LINDB art. 11 par. 2, par. 3 (src:47-48)
GIVEN `it is a foreign government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an organisation a foreign government constituted, directs or has invested with public functions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is real property or susceptible to expropriation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the building is needed for the seat of diplomatic representatives or consular agents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a foreign government or its organisation may acquire the property in Brazil` `it is a foreign government` `it is an organisation a foreign government constituted, directs or has invested with public functions` `the property is real property or susceptible to expropriation` `the building is needed for the seat of diplomatic representatives or consular agents` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `art. 11 par. 3 allows the acquisition` `it is a foreign government` `the building is needed for the seat of diplomatic representatives or consular agents` THEN TRUE
        IF `art. 11 par. 2 forbids the acquisition` `it is a foreign government` `it is an organisation a foreign government constituted, directs or has invested with public functions` `the property is real property or susceptible to expropriation` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE `neither par. 2 nor par. 3 of art. 11 speaks to this acquisition`

§§ `Art. 12: the competence of the Brazilian judicial authority`

-- src:49 | Art. 12. É competente a autoridade judiciária brasileira, quando for o réu domiciliado no Brasil ou aqui tiver de ser cumprida a obrigação.
-- src:50 | § 1o Só à autoridade judiciária brasileira compete conhecer das ações relativas a imóveis situados no Brasil.
-- src:51 | § 2o A autoridade judiciária brasileira cumprirá, concedido o exequatur e segundo a forma estabelecida pela lei brasileira, as diligências deprecadas por autoridade estrangeira competente, observando a lei desta, quanto ao objeto das diligências.
@ref LINDB art. 12 caput to par. 2 (src:49-51)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`art. 12 caput names two grounds and does not say whether there are others` MEANS
    REFUSE "art. 12 caput names two grounds of competence and the text does not say whether there are others"

-- The Brazilian judicial authority is competent when the defendant is domiciled in Brazil or the obligation is to be performed here.
-- TRUE when a listed ground holds. Where neither holds the text does not say that the authority is not competent: refused.
@ref LINDB art. 12 caput (src:49)
GIVEN `the defendant is domiciled in Brazil` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the obligation is to be performed in Brazil` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Brazilian judicial authority is competent on a ground listed in art. 12 caput` `the defendant is domiciled in Brazil` `the obligation is to be performed in Brazil` MEANS
    IF `the defendant is domiciled in Brazil` OR `the obligation is to be performed in Brazil`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `art. 12 caput names two grounds and does not say whether there are others`

-- Par. 1: only the Brazilian judicial authority may hear actions relating to immovables situated in Brazil.
@ref LINDB art. 12 par. 1 (src:50)
GIVEN `the action relates to immovable property situated in Brazil` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`only the Brazilian judicial authority may hear the action, under art. 12 par. 1` `the action relates to immovable property situated in Brazil` MEANS
    `the action relates to immovable property situated in Brazil`

-- Par. 2: letters rogatory from a competent foreign authority are carried out by the Brazilian judicial authority once the
-- exequatur is granted, in the form Brazilian law lays down and observing the foreign law as to the object of the measures.
@ref LINDB art. 12 par. 2 (src:51)
GIVEN `the request comes from a competent foreign authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exequatur has been granted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Brazilian judicial authority carries out the letter rogatory under art. 12 par. 2` `the request comes from a competent foreign authority` `the exequatur has been granted` MEANS
    `the request comes from a competent foreign authority` AND `the exequatur has been granted`

@ref LINDB art. 12 par. 2 (src:51)
GIVETH A STRING
`the country whose law governs the form of carrying out a letter rogatory` MEANS "Brazil"

@ref LINDB art. 12 par. 2 (src:51)
GIVEN `the country of the requesting authority` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`the country whose law governs the object of the measures of a letter rogatory from` `the country of the requesting authority` MEANS
    `the country of the requesting authority`

§§ `Arts. 13 and 14: foreign facts and foreign law`

-- src:52 | Art. 13. A prova dos fatos ocorridos em país estrangeiro rege-se pela lei que nele vigorar, quanto ao ônus e aos meios de produzir-se, não admitindo os tribunais brasileiros provas que a lei brasileira desconheça.
@ref LINDB art. 13 (src:52)
GIVEN `the country where the fact occurred` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`the country whose law governs the burden and the means of proving a fact that occurred in` `the country where the fact occurred` MEANS
    `the country where the fact occurred`

-- Brazilian courts do not admit proofs that Brazilian law does not know, whatever the law of the place says about the means.
@ref LINDB art. 13 (src:52)
GIVEN `the law of the place where the fact occurred admits the means of proof` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Brazilian law knows the means of proof` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a Brazilian court admits the means of proof of a fact that occurred abroad` `the law of the place where the fact occurred admits the means of proof` `Brazilian law knows the means of proof` MEANS
        `the law of the place where the fact occurred admits the means of proof`
    AND `Brazilian law knows the means of proof`

-- src:53 | Art. 14. Não conhecendo a lei estrangeira, poderá o juiz exigir de quem a invoca prova do texto e da vigência.
@ref LINDB art. 14 (src:53)
GIVEN `the judge knows the foreign law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 14 allows the judge to require of the party invoking it proof of the text and force of the foreign law` `the judge knows the foreign law` MEANS
    NOT `the judge knows the foreign law`

§§ `Art. 15: a foreign judgment executed in Brazil`

-- src:54 | Art. 15. Será executada no Brasil a sentença proferida no estrangeiro, que reuna os seguintes requisitos:
-- src:55 | a) haver sido proferida por juiz competente;
-- src:56 | b) terem sido os partes citadas ou haver-se legalmente verificado à revelia;
-- src:57 | c) ter passado em julgado e estar revestida das formalidades necessárias para a execução no lugar em que foi proferida;
-- src:58 | d) estar traduzida por intérprete autorizado;
-- src:59 | e) ter sido homologada pelo Supremo Tribunal Federal.
-- src:60 | Parágrafo único. (Revogado pela Lei nº 12.036, de 2009).
@ref LINDB art. 15 caput, a to e, sole paragraph (src:54-60)
DECLARE `A foreign judgment, for art. 15` HAS
    `it was given by a competent judge`                                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parties were served`                                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `default was legally verified`                                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `it has become res judicata`                                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `it has the formalities necessary for execution in the place where it was given`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is translated by an authorised interpreter`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `it has been homologated by the Supremo Tribunal Federal`                                          IS A BOOLEAN

-- The five requirements of art. 15 caput. (b) is met by service or by default legally verified; (c) needs both limbs.
-- Art. 15 names the Supremo Tribunal Federal in (e) while art. 7 par. 6 names the Superior Tribunal de Justica; the text does not
-- reconcile the two (open question Q-3), and (e) is carried as the text has it.
@ref LINDB art. 15 caput, a to e (src:54-59)
GIVEN j IS A `A foreign judgment, for art. 15`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the foreign judgment meets the requirements of art. 15` j MEANS
        "a)" ... j's `it was given by a competent judge`
    AND "b)" ... (j's `the parties were served` OR j's `default was legally verified`)
    AND "c)" ... j's `it has become res judicata`
              AND j's `it has the formalities necessary for execution in the place where it was given`
    AND "d)" ... j's `it is translated by an authorised interpreter`
    AND "e)" ... j's `it has been homologated by the Supremo Tribunal Federal`

§§ `Arts. 16 and 17: renvoi, and what offends`

-- src:61 | Art. 16. Quando, nos termos dos artigos precedentes, se houver de aplicar a lei estrangeira, ter-se-á em vista a disposição desta, sem considerar-se qualquer remissão por ela feita a outra lei.
@ref LINDB art. 16 (src:61)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a foreign law's remission to another law is considered` MEANS FALSE

-- src:62 | Art. 17. As leis, atos e sentenças de outro país, bem como quaisquer declarações de vontade, não terão eficácia no Brasil, quando ofenderem a soberania nacional, a ordem pública e os bons costumes.
-- Art. 17 reads "a soberania nacional, a ordem publica e os bons costumes" as a list of what is offended. Any one is taken to be enough
-- (fork F-17): the cumulative reading, that all three must be offended at once, is the one rejected.
@ref LINDB art. 17 (src:62)
GIVEN `it offends national sovereignty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it offends public order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it offends good morals` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 17 denies the foreign law, act, judgment or declaration of will efficacy in Brazil` `it offends national sovereignty` `it offends public order` `it offends good morals` MEANS
        `it offends national sovereignty`
     OR `it offends public order`
     OR `it offends good morals`

§§ `Arts. 18 and 19: the consular authorities`

-- src:63 | Art. 18. Tratando-se de brasileiros, são competentes as autoridades consulares brasileiras para lhes celebrar o casamento e os mais atos de Registro Civil e de tabelionato, inclusive o registro de nascimento e de óbito dos filhos de brasileiro ou brasileira nascido no país da sede do Consulado.
-- src:64 | § 1º As autoridades consulares brasileiras também poderão celebrar a separação consensual e o divórcio consensual de brasileiros, não havendo filhos menores ou incapazes do casal e observados os requisitos legais quanto aos prazos, devendo constar da respectiva escritura pública as disposições relativas à descrição e à partilha dos bens comuns e à pensão alimentícia e, ainda, ao acordo quanto à retomada pelo cônjuge de seu nome de solteiro ou à manutenção do nome adotado quando se deu o casamento.
-- src:65 | § 2o É indispensável a assistência de advogado, devidamente constituído, que se dará mediante a subscrição de petição, juntamente com ambas as partes, ou com apenas uma delas, caso a outra constitua advogado próprio, não se fazendo necessário que a assinatura do advogado conste da escritura pública.
@ref LINDB art. 18 caput to par. 2 (src:63-65)
DECLARE `Act for which art. 18 caput makes the consular authority competent` IS ONE OF
    `the celebration of a marriage`
    `another act of civil registry`
    `a notarial act`
    `the registration of the birth of a child of a Brazilian born in the country where the consulate sits`
    `the registration of the death of a child of a Brazilian born in the country where the consulate sits`

@ref LINDB art. 18 caput (src:63)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`art. 18 caput speaks only of acts concerning Brazilians` MEANS
    REFUSE "art. 18 caput speaks only of acts concerning Brazilians and says nothing of the consular authority's competence for others"

-- Caput: for Brazilians, the Brazilian consular authorities are competent for these acts. The kind of act is one of the listed
-- constructors, so an act outside the list cannot be asked about; for an act concerning someone who is not Brazilian the text is silent.
@ref LINDB art. 18 caput (src:63)
GIVEN act IS A `Act for which art. 18 caput makes the consular authority competent`
      `it concerns Brazilians` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Brazilian consular authority is competent under art. 18 caput for` act `when` `it concerns Brazilians` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `the celebration of a marriage` THEN `art. 18 caput applies` `it concerns Brazilians`
    WHEN `another act of civil registry` THEN `art. 18 caput applies` `it concerns Brazilians`
    WHEN `a notarial act` THEN `art. 18 caput applies` `it concerns Brazilians`
    WHEN `the registration of the birth of a child of a Brazilian born in the country where the consulate sits` THEN `art. 18 caput applies` `it concerns Brazilians`
    WHEN `the registration of the death of a child of a Brazilian born in the country where the consulate sits` THEN `art. 18 caput applies` `it concerns Brazilians`

@ref LINDB art. 18 caput (src:63)
GIVEN `it concerns Brazilians` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 18 caput applies` `it concerns Brazilians` MEANS
    IF `it concerns Brazilians` THEN TRUE ELSE `art. 18 caput speaks only of acts concerning Brazilians`

-- Par. 1: the consular authorities may also celebrate a consensual separation and a consensual divorce of Brazilians where there are
-- no minor or incapable children of the couple, the legal requirements as to periods are observed, and the public deed records the
-- provisions on the description and partition of the common property, on maintenance, and on the agreement about the spouse's name.
@ref LINDB art. 18 par. 1 (src:64)
GIVEN `the spouses are Brazilians` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the separation or divorce is consensual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are no minor or incapable children of the couple` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the legal requirements as to periods are observed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deed records the description and partition of the common property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deed records the maintenance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deed records the agreement on retaking the maiden name or keeping the married name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 18 par. 1 allows the consular authority to celebrate` `the spouses are Brazilians` `the separation or divorce is consensual` `there are no minor or incapable children of the couple` `the legal requirements as to periods are observed` `the deed records the description and partition of the common property` `the deed records the maintenance` `the deed records the agreement on retaking the maiden name or keeping the married name` MEANS
        `the spouses are Brazilians`
    AND `the separation or divorce is consensual`
    AND `there are no minor or incapable children of the couple`
    AND `the legal requirements as to periods are observed`
    AND `the deed records the description and partition of the common property`
    AND `the deed records the maintenance`
    AND `the deed records the agreement on retaking the maiden name or keeping the married name`

-- Par. 2: the assistance of a duly constituted lawyer is indispensable, given by subscribing the petition together with both
-- parties, or with only one of them if the other constitutes their own lawyer. The lawyer's signature on the deed is not required.
@ref LINDB art. 18 par. 2 (src:65)
GIVEN `a lawyer duly constituted assisted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lawyer subscribed the petition together with both parties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lawyer subscribed the petition together with one party and the other party constituted their own lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the assistance of a lawyer required by art. 18 par. 2 is given` `a lawyer duly constituted assisted` `the lawyer subscribed the petition together with both parties` `the lawyer subscribed the petition together with one party and the other party constituted their own lawyer` MEANS
        `a lawyer duly constituted assisted`
    AND (   `the lawyer subscribed the petition together with both parties`
         OR `the lawyer subscribed the petition together with one party and the other party constituted their own lawyer`)

@ref LINDB art. 18 par. 2 (src:65)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the lawyer's signature on the public deed is required` MEANS FALSE

-- src:66 | Art. 19. Reputam-se válidos todos os atos indicados no artigo anterior e celebrados pelos cônsules brasileiros na vigência do Decreto-lei nº 4.657, de 4 de setembro de 1942, desde que satisfaçam todos os requisitos legais.
-- src:67 | Parágrafo único. No caso em que a celebração dêsses atos tiver sido recusada pelas autoridades consulares, com fundamento no artigo 18 do mesmo Decreto-lei, ao interessado é facultado renovar o pedido dentro em 90 (noventa) dias contados da data da publicação desta lei.
-- Art. 19 caput validates the acts of art. 18 celebrated by Brazilian consuls while the Decreto-Lei was in force, if they met every legal
-- requirement. The period "na vigencia" is not given in this text (open question Q-4), so it is a fact the caller supplies.
@ref LINDB art. 19 caput, sole paragraph (src:66-67)
GIVEN `the act is one indicated in art. 18` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was celebrated by a Brazilian consul while the Decreto-Lei was in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it satisfied every legal requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 19 caput validates the act` `the act is one indicated in art. 18` `it was celebrated by a Brazilian consul while the Decreto-Lei was in force` `it satisfied every legal requirement` MEANS
        `the act is one indicated in art. 18`
    AND `it was celebrated by a Brazilian consul while the Decreto-Lei was in force`
    AND `it satisfied every legal requirement`

-- The sole paragraph: where the consular authorities refused to celebrate on the basis of art. 18, the interested person may renew the
-- request within 90 days counted from the date of publication of "this law" (which law that is is not said, open question Q-4).
-- The window is answered only where both readings of "counted from" agree: the first and the 90th day after the publication are refused.
@ref LINDB art. 19 sole paragraph (src:67)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the date of publication of this law` IS A DATE
      `the consular authorities had refused on the basis of art. 18` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 19 sole paragraph allows the request to be renewed on` d `the date of publication of this law` `the consular authorities had refused on the basis of art. 18` MEANS
    IF `the consular authorities had refused on the basis of art. 18`
    THEN `the day` d `falls inside a period of` 90 `days counted from` `the date of publication of this law`
    ELSE FALSE
